unknown format: no-format

Usage:
  fakedata [options] [column-spec...]

Examples:
  fakedata email:int:1,100 name:full_name        generate 10 rows with two columns
  fakedata -n 5 -f ndjson city country           5 rows in NDJSON format

Column spec syntax: [name:][generator[:args]]
  email                    column "email" using email generator
  int:10,20                column "int" with range 10-20
  login:email              column "login" using email generator
  count:int:10,20          column "count" using int generator, range 10-20

Use `fakedata --help <topic>` for detailed help on columns, formats, seeding, templates.


Utility
  -h, --help                   show this help; use --help <topic> for detailed guides
  -v, --version                show version information
  -C, --completion string      print shell completion function ("bash", "zsh", "fish")

Column mode
  -f, --format string          output format: column|ndjson (default column)
  -H, --header                 print a header row with column names
  -n, --rows int               number of rows to generate (default 10)
  -s, --separator string       field separator for column format (default "\t")
    --seed int                 seed for deterministic random generation (default 0)
  -S, --stream                 stream rows indefinitely
  -T, --template string        template file to execute

Discovery
  -g, --generator string       show details and examples for a generator
  -G, --generators             list available generators
